  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the national response for the control of Tuberculosis and  supporting the strengthening of the health system in Angola - Angola (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Angola, Tuberculosis, Ministry of Health of the Republic of Angola (MOH)This program has the following goals: Reduce TB incidence by 20% by 2021 compared to 2015 level.  Reduce TB mortality by 35% by 2021 compared to 2015 level. The objectives of this program are: Detect 80% of the estimated TB cases (all forms) and achieve a treatment success rate of 79% of TB cases (all forms) by 2021..  Increase the detection rate of MDR TB to 75% by 2021 and treat diagnosed MDR TB cases..  Expand TB/HIV collaborative activities by ensuring that 75% of notified TB patients are tested for HIV and 80% who test HIV positive are put on ART promptly by 2021..  Strengthen the M&amp;E system to ensure all indicators listed are tracked and reported timely.</narrative>
  </description>
